// Title: PUA - Potential PE Metadata Tamper Using Rcedit
// ID: 0c92f2e6-f08f-4b73-9216-ecb0ca634689
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Micah Babinski
// Date: 2022-12-11
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1036.003, attack.t1036, attack.t1027.005, attack.t1027
// Description: Detects the use of rcedit to potentially alter executable PE metadata properties, which could conceal efforts to rename system utilities for defense evasion.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "OriginalFileName") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "CompanyName") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "FileDescription") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "ProductName") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "ProductVersion") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "LegalCopyright"))) AND (where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "--set-")) AND (((where(Image IENDSWITH "\\rcedit-x64.exe") OR where(Image IENDSWITH "\\rcedit-x86.exe"))) OR (where(Description = "Edit resources of exe")) OR (where(Product = "rcedit"))))
